{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Enoch son of Jared.</b> It is written about him, \"Enoch walked with Elohim,\" like the sense of \"After YHWH your Elohim you shall walk\" (Deuteronomy 13:5), and similarly it is written about Noah, \"Noah walked with Elohim\" (Genesis 6:9). And some say \"walked, Noah\" is in the usual sense [of habit]."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:22.485065233Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}